A||||5||Fret Naught||I did it||||7||
Z||000000||Fret Naught||05-26-2000||10:22 PM||||Well I went ahead and did it, I painted a BRA on my car, I didn't like the look of the one I just bought, to cover up all of the rock chips ect..., I went to a place called industrial coatings, picked up a quart of pickup bed liner, rented their special gun, and did it. I think it looks great, it should be fully cured tomorrow, it stays flexiable, and has a chemical in it that is supposed to keep it from fading. Had I been thinking ahead, I would have pulled the mirrors and done them as well. Anybody want a slightly used Bra cheap? The whole job took me about 2 hours, and cost $48.00.||||reg||7
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-26-2000||10:26 PM||||Why not just repaint the front nose?||||reg||5
Z||000002||Fret Naught||05-26-2000||10:51 PM||||Two reasons 1. I am not that good with paint, it is not a stock color, and I was worried that I would not be able to blend it properly. I wasn't real excited about paying the local shop 500.00 to do it.<BR>2. I wanted something that would resist stone chips, this is my daily driver, and it gets a lot of road time, New paint just makes room for new chips. This way I figured I could have the best of both worlds it actually looks like a shrink to fit bra.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||05-26-2000||11:06 PM||||There is a spray stuff called chip guard that goes on clear and is real tough to prevent those rock chips.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||05-27-2000||12:49 AM||||sounds interesting.. be sure to post pics!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||05-27-2000||01:45 AM||||Several of my coworkers have sprayed their rocker panels with bedliner and it works very well, it is TOUGH!  The Fiero is next, lucky for me it is already black.<BR>The stuff is just fantastic, deadens sound and vibration also, like bulletproof undercoating.<BR>And if the pebbly look just doesn't fit the decor then the texture can be left out completely or adjusted anywhere from shiny to sandpaper.<P>Of course compared to a genuine car finish this looks like latex put on with a roller.||||reg||12
